    <statement><p>Use the chain rule to find <m>\frac{dz}{dt}</m>, where 
<me>z = x^2 y + x y^2,\quad  x = 3 - t^7,\quad y = 5 + t^3</me></p>
<p>First the pieces:</p>
<p><m>\frac{\partial z}{\partial x} =</m> <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><m>\frac{\partial z}{\partial y} =</m> <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p><m>\frac{dx}{dt} =</m> <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
<p><m>\frac{dy}{dt} =</m> <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
<p>End result (in terms of just <m>t</m>):</p>
<p><m>\frac{dz}{dt} =</m> <fillin characters="60" name="AnSwEr0005"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2xy+y^{2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>x^{2}+2xy</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-7t^{6}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3t^{2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(2\mathopen{}\left(3+\left(-1\right)t^{7}\right)\mathopen{}\left(5+1t^{3}\right)+\left(5+1t^{3}\right)^{2}\right)\mathopen{}\left(-1\right)\cdot 7t^{6}+\left(2\mathopen{}\left(3+\left(-1\right)t^{7}\right)\mathopen{}\left(5+1t^{3}\right)+\left(3+\left(-1\right)t^{7}\right)^{2}\right)\cdot 1\cdot 3t^{2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
